Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.31,0:00:14.13,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.26,0:00:19.12,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Am I... in water?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.22,0:00:26.63,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,What are these lights?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.26,0:00:33.62,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,A giant fish?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.79,0:00:37.64,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,No... a dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.64,0:00:39.16,Sign_Basic,Dragon Illdoren,0,0,0,,{\shad0\bord0\fnArial\pos(320,324)\c&HE7E7E7&\fs18} Sera....
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.16,0:00:43.14,Sign_Basic,Dragon Illdoren,0,0,0,,{\shad0\bord0\fnArial\c&HE7E7E7&\fs18\pos(320,324)}I am glad I chose you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.57,0:00:44.46,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.25,0:00:54.35,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Wait! What do you mean by—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.11,0:01:00.20,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It was a dream?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.98,0:01:03.19,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But why...?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.88,0:01:05.85,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,How could a dragon talk?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.85,0:01:08.84,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,And such a massive creature...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.02,0:01:11.37,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,I've never seen or heard \Nof anything like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.37,0:01:14.73,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Did the Morisuberi we hunted show \Nup in my dreams, or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.73,0:01:16.72,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,Get off...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.72,0:01:19.97,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,Illdoren, you're gonna \Nsqueeze my guts out...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.21,0:01:23.16,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,L-Lady Vyufmec?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.91,0:01:48.55,Sign_Basic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(2500,1725)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFAFDFE&\3c&H3D6671&\4c&H372771&\shad2}T{\c&HF8FCFD&}h{\c&HF6FBFC&}e{\c&HF4FAFB&} {\c&HF2F9FA&}W{\c&HF1F8FA&}a{\c&HEFF7F9&}r{\c&HEDF6F8&}r{\c&HEBF5F7&}i{\c&HE9F4F6&}o{\c&HE7F3F5&}r{\c&HE5F2F4&} {\c&HE3F1F3&}P{\c&HE2F0F3&}r{\c&HE0EFF2&}i{\c&HDEEEF1&}n{\c&HDCEDF0&}c{\c&HDAECEF&}e{\c&HD8EBEE&}s{\c&HD6EAED&}s{\c&HD4E9EC&} {\c&HD3E7EC&}a{\c&HD1E6EB&}n{\c&HCFE5EA&}d{\c&HCDE4E9&} {\c&HCBE3E8&}t{\c&HC9E2E7&}h{\c&HC7E1E6&}e{\c&HC5E0E5&} {\c&HC4DFE5&}B{\c&HC2DEE4&}a{\c&HC0DDE3&}r{\c&HBEDCE2&}b{\c&HBCDBE1&}a{\c&HBADAE0&}r{\c&HB8D9DF&}i{\c&HB6D8DE&}c{\c&HB5D7DE&} {\c&HB3D6DD&}K{\c&HB1D5DC&}i{\c&HAFD4DB&}n{\c&HADD3DA&}g
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.28,0:03:05.97,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,There are elves and dwarves \Nfrom out of a fairy tale,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.97,0:03:08.66,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,along with some \Nmenacing-looking living plants...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.66,0:03:13.13,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,You are so obnoxious.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.46,0:03:17.13,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Wh-Why am I being forced to deal with \Nbarbarians and inhuman creatures?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.52,0:03:21.13,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I already told you; today we're \Nperforming the great cleansing ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.81,0:03:26.35,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Which is why the five tribes have \Ngathered so early in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.35,0:03:31.57,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,E-Even, so, how do you expect me to accept \Nsomething so egregiously fantastical?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.45,0:03:37.05,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Y'know, in the short time I've known \Nyou, it's clear how fanatical you are...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.05,0:03:40.47,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,But do you really think that the \Nonly things that exist in this world
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.47,0:03:42.53,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,are the things that you \Npersonally find believable?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.91,0:03:46.26,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,Hey, the gang's all here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.26,0:03:48.29,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Saint Wysteresia!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.67,0:03:51.91,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,You're responsible for \Nthe blight, this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.69,0:03:56.31,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,So you're going to participate in our \Ntradition of the great cleansing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.31,0:03:57.79,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.79,0:03:59.55,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Cleansed though you may be,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.88,0:04:04.93,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,it's important you personally \Nsee the results of your actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.36,0:04:06.93,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Cleansed?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.66,0:04:09.74,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,She doesn't even realize it...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.74,0:04:11.73,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Say that again, elf?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.73,0:04:14.73,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,What name did your parents give you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.66,0:04:18.10,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,You want my name?! What for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.10,0:04:19.57,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Let's just hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.57,0:04:23.93,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Well, I got the surname \Nof Malcius from the abbot,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.93,0:04:28.02,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,seven years ago when I \Nbecame a retinue priest...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.46,0:04:29.49,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.81,0:04:33.25,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,What did they call me at \Nthe orphanage again...?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.25,0:04:36.75,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,I know that becoming a retinue \Npriest at 16 was unprecedented...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.75,0:04:41.26,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,But prior to that? Sixteen years...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.26,0:04:43.20,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,You don't remember any of it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.20,0:04:45.49,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,And 16 years would be \Nthe majority of your life!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.49,0:04:47.09,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Th-That can't be right!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.29,0:04:52.88,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,I can remember six years \Nago... seven years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.88,0:04:58.77,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Eight years ago... nothing? \NNothing, nothing, nothing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.77,0:05:00.82,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Whoa, Malcius!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.82,0:05:02.41,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,It's an effect of the blight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.42,0:05:07.69,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,It's honestly a miracle she \Nsurvived in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.69,0:05:12.69,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,True. You could say that losing \Nher memories is a small price.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.69,0:05:15.33,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Though I doubt she'd agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.60,0:05:18.54,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,This might be insensitive,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.54,0:05:21.30,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,but maybe forgetting about the \Nmemories of being a slave to religion
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.30,0:05:23.34,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,would be better for her...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.77,0:05:23.65,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Wha?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.45,0:05:27.58,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Wh-Wh-What did you just say?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.58,0:05:31.87,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,You think I'd be better off forgetting \Nmy devotion to the Lord?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.87,0:05:33.96,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,H-How dare you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.96,0:05:36.41,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Then try and remember something.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.41,0:05:40.56,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Assuming there were any thoughts \Nin your head to remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.83,0:05:46.32,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Y-Y-You just keep running \Nyour mouth, you little wench!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.57,0:05:49.91,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I only stated the truth, \Nyou freckled four-eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.91,0:05:53.70,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,My a-a-appearance has nothing \Nto do with my religion!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.97,0:05:57.46,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,They met a few days ago and \Nlook how they get along...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.46,0:06:00.22,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Hard to say if they're compatible, or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.22,0:06:01.96,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we do something?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.96,0:06:05.21,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I doubt it'll escalate \Ninto anything dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.67,0:06:08.72,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,And if it does, I'll stop them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.72,0:06:10.51,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,Yeah, fight, fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.18,0:06:15.43,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,You start a fight, and are \Nalready on the ground?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.43,0:06:20.23,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,You were the one who was \Nmocking me, barbarian girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.52,0:06:27.57,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Don't take a retinue priest with the \NE-E-Eastern Expedition forces lightly!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.57,0:06:30.53,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,All that marching has made me fit!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.53,0:06:32.62,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Ow! Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.62,0:06:35.75,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,You might've been able \Nto get the drop on me,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.75,0:06:38.90,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,but if you really think I'm \Nbetter off without my memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.90,0:06:40.62,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,then how about this, little barbarian?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.10,0:06:44.75,Flashback,Cersei,0,0,0,,I might hate what the \NOrder of Commoneras stands for,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.06,0:06:47.76,Flashback,Cersei,0,0,0,,but I did receive some \Ncharity from them once...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.38,0:06:51.95,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,I forgot to mention this earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.95,0:06:56.52,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,but did you know that this \Nbarbarian-styled girl is actually—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.99,0:07:05.02,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,She's got her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.01,0:07:10.78,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Bar...bar...ian...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.01,0:07:17.04,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,We have a winner!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.04,0:07:19.82,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I suppose I'll carry Malcius...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.09,0:07:24.65,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,Why don't the three of you \Nrun down to the river, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.27,0:07:28.45,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,There's still time before \Nthe great cleansing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.45,0:07:31.78,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,It'll be a good chance to get in \Nthe water and clean up a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.78,0:07:36.43,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,A good suggestion. A wash before \Nthe ritual would do you well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.43,0:07:37.99,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.99,0:07:40.93,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,The preparations will go\N just fine without you three.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.55,0:07:43.81,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,I mean, it's not like \Nyou have anything to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.70,0:07:47.17,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,Don't feel bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.17,0:07:51.93,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,I'm going to spend the ritual relaxing \Nat my nephew's house, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.93,0:07:53.29,Main,Wysteresia,0,0,0,,I'm too old for this shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.29,0:07:54.78,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Resia...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.78,0:07:58.33,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You heard her, Cersei. \NSee them to the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.94,0:08:00.08,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.33,0:08:06.63,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I'm sure you noticed, \Nfrom what this fanatic nearly said...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.34,0:08:10.37,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,And it's true. I am from Illdoren.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.37,0:08:13.84,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I was part of the Eastern \NCultivation Corps, six years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.53,0:08:16.04,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I thought as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.04,0:08:19.38,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Your disdain for nobles, and the fact that
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.38,0:08:23.27,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,you called me a knight instead of \Na warrior had caught my notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.87,0:08:27.88,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That said, I'd imagine learning \Nhow to help equip armor
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.88,0:08:30.61,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,didn't come from being in \Nthe Cultivation Corp...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.88,0:08:36.32,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I'd ask you not to pry any further. \NThat country isn't my home anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.32,0:08:40.49,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I am Cersei, Master Veor's attendant, \Nand these lands are where I belong.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.45,0:08:45.45,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I treat you as the woman my \Nmaster has chosen to court.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.45,0:08:48.50,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,So please, do not start treating \Nme as a citizen of Illdoren.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.19,0:08:51.51,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I would never...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.34,0:08:55.62,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Well, you may have a point. \NI'll be more careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.12,0:08:59.15,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Cersei...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.15,0:09:00.01,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.54,0:09:06.52,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Are the memories of our homeland... \Nsomething you would rather forget?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.56,0:09:17.28,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Well... it's more like I don't remember, \Nanyway. And can't be bothered to.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.30,0:09:21.18,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Since I never intend on going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.29,0:09:28.04,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,H-How could I, a retinue priest, \Nbe so careless?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.04,0:09:30.02,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I understand how you feel,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.02,0:09:33.37,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,but you would've been stuck like \Nthat unless someone said something.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.05,0:09:37.15,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,While it's true that my \Nmemories might be... hazy...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.15,0:09:40.55,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,It looked like you'd mutter\N to yourself for the rest of your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.55,0:09:42.31,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,S-S-Say what?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.51,0:09:45.56,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Just calm down, Malcius.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.56,0:09:48.65,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Could someone explain why \NI'm on an errand
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.65,0:09:50.91,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,with the girl I was wrestling with?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.91,0:09:53.94,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,I might be willing to accompany \Nthis barbarian girl
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.94,0:09:57.79,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,since I can't leave your side, \NLady Serafina, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.79,0:09:59.48,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Because you stink.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.20,0:10:02.87,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,What did you just say?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.72,0:10:06.62,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Are you saying I s-s-stink?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.26,0:10:09.75,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Yes, you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.75,0:10:12.17,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I'm sure you haven't noticed yourself,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.17,0:10:15.84,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,but it's a mixture of blood, sweat,\Na bit sour, and some faint perfume.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.91,0:10:19.96,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I have to wonder how long\Nit's been since you last bathed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.09,0:10:22.83,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.25,0:10:27.72,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Well, it was four days before \NLady Serafina served as the vanguard,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.72,0:10:30.60,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,and was captured the barbarians...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.78,0:10:36.62,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Over half a month?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.25,0:10:43.14,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Malcius... it's just... well...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.48,0:10:44.97,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,There was never a good time...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.97,0:10:47.62,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,and I do feel bad for \Nnot saying anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.12,0:10:48.93,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.58,0:10:50.62,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.45,0:10:58.10,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That said, I've worked up quite a \Nsweat over these last two or three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.99,0:11:01.22,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,This might be perfect timing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.05,0:11:05.34,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I'll keep my sword nearby, \Njust in case we need it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.34,0:11:08.14,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I really doubt you need to worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.54,0:11:17.86,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,This area around the mountain by the \Nvillage is Master Veor's territory,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.13,0:11:20.26,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,so dragons don't come around here often.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.26,0:11:24.00,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,E-Even if they're rare, you still bathe \Nin places dragons have been seen?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.00,0:11:27.29,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Well, anywhere else would \Nbe actual dragon territory,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.29,0:11:30.37,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,as I'm sure you saw in the western woods.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.21,0:11:33.23,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,I want to go back west...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.23,0:11:35.13,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Malcius.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.54,0:11:44.28,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But like I told you before, I don't \Nintend on leaving here any time soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.69,0:11:51.25,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I'd recommend cleaning up quickly. \NYou don't want to catch a chill.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.21,0:11:54.03,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.12,0:11:59.59,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Lady Serafina?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.71,0:12:13.71,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,A campfire after a bath can be quite nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.66,0:12:19.21,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Cleaning off does lose its charm \Nif you're freezing from the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.23,0:12:21.74,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,It's warm...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.43,0:12:25.71,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I think they're just about done.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.07,0:12:29.47,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Yes, it looks like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.70,0:12:38.99,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,It's good...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.49,0:12:51.11,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I suppose it's time for \Nthis great cleansing...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.45,0:12:57.47,Main,Balhath,0,0,0,,Gotta say, it's real good the blight \Nwas purged as fast as it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.47,0:12:59.02,Main,Guas,0,0,0,,If it's still in its cocoon,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.02,0:13:01.90,Main,Guas,0,0,0,,the cleansing is easier to set up, \Nand easier to do!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.90,0:13:04.28,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,I heard the new bride took it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.28,0:13:06.64,Main,Guas,0,0,0,,Talk about bold. Couldn't be me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.22,0:13:10.51,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I can't believe how much the \Nstory has spread in one day...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.51,0:13:14.01,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,Oh, we worked hard to make \Nit happen, believe me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.98,0:13:21.26,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, Malcius landed \Non your head, knocking you both out...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.26,0:13:25.28,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I-I'm not usually that careless! \NI didn't have a helmet, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.77,0:13:28.82,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Besides, I dare you to find \Nanyone who doesn't relax
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.82,0:13:30.28,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,after slaying something like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.93,0:13:34.03,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I suppose you're right about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.03,0:13:39.93,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,And while Illdoren was knocked \Nout, we were flying all around!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.93,0:13:41.26,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,And now, I'm exhausted!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.26,0:13:45.01,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That sounds like quite the ordeal. \NThank you for your efforts.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.25,0:13:48.35,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,Well, the truth is, I don't \Nreally know what exhaustion is.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.93,0:13:53.06,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You see, Sera, because the Tefyu \Nare more like natural phenomenon,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.06,0:13:54.93,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,their perception is bit \Ndifferent from ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.28,0:13:59.52,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,She might even have trouble \Ntelling Cersei and Malcius apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.52,0:14:02.94,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That seems like more than "a bit."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.79,0:14:04.57,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,What's it matter,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.57,0:14:07.33,Main,Vyu,0,0,0,,as long as I can tell the difference \Nbetween important people?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.33,0:14:10.31,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That's starting to sound \Nmore like disinterest...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.28,0:14:13.70,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,Here we are!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.90,0:14:17.24,Main,Dwarves{not marked as distinct},0,0,0,,There it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.24,0:14:19.83,Main,Dwarves{not marked as distinct},0,0,0,,What a mess...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.51,0:14:38.35,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.60,0:14:41.67,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Wh-Wh-What the? \NIt's like it's been bleached...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.49,0:14:53.35,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,This is... white dust?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.27,0:14:59.40,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,The area where we fought the \NFiend has turned to dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.18,0:15:02.33,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Another effect of the blight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.88,0:15:05.47,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The same way that we all have wills,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.47,0:15:09.02,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,the earth, water, flame, \Nand wind do as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.47,0:15:12.03,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,And while they're all similiar in nature,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.03,0:15:15.18,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,there's one fundamental difference between
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.18,0:15:18.02,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,the will of living creatures \Nand any other kind....
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.69,0:15:23.26,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,When a life is depleted of willpower, \Nit simply never returns.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.26,0:15:27.74,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,But for for everything else... \Nfor nature itself, willpower stagnates,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.74,0:15:30.55,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,grows corrupt, forgetting its \Nintended state, and turns to dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.78,0:15:34.73,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Or so I was told\Nby our resident Rijutsushi,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.73,0:15:36.87,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Karka Roth, several years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.87,0:15:37.55,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Hello!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.34,0:15:42.46,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,It sounded really convincing...\Nbut it was all just second-hand knowledge?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.99,0:15:40.50,Main - Top,Roth,0,0,0,,Hey there!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.85,0:15:46.51,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,I suppose I can go into \Ngreater detail, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.51,0:15:52.88,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,But first, I'd like to see the tool \Nof the fool who caused this mess.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.39,0:15:57.01,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Here it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.83,0:16:01.73,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Th-That's my scripture!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.73,0:16:02.69,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Give it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.69,0:16:04.60,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Thief...!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.61,0:16:10.18,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,A rijutsu text, primarily focused \Non converting things to light,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.18,0:16:11.61,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,heat, and impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.93,0:16:13.67,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I thought as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.67,0:16:16.49,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Indeed. Completely lacking in artistry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.49,0:16:20.88,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,B-But it seemed dangerous \Nenough to do real damage
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.88,0:16:23.50,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,if one wasn't wearing armor...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.50,0:16:28.03,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,It used enough of the land's willpower \Nto leave it in this state, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.03,0:16:30.67,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,There's no arguing against its potency.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.67,0:16:32.18,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,But from our point of view,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.18,0:16:37.26,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,the very idea of using rijutsu for \Ndestruction is inherently crude.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.16,0:16:45.21,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Now, then, it's almost noon. \NWith weather this pleasant,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.21,0:16:47.40,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,it should prove a nice \Nwake-up call, for the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.89,0:16:56.07,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What are those?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.07,0:16:59.66,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Catalysts. Brought in by \Nthe different clans...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.66,0:17:03.54,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Offering earth, water, \Nfire, and wind catalysts
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.54,0:17:05.42,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,along with a prayer acts as an excitation
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.94,0:17:09.17,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,to help the land recall its true nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.06,0:17:25.50,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Let's begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.27,0:17:43.45,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,In the name of the great spirits, we will\Nnow perform the great cleansing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.93,0:17:49.88,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Vesenem kehfem kehnakyahne fonehda.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.81,0:17:56.62,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Something about his words sounded older \Nthan any language I'd ever heard,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.11,0:17:59.82,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,as they echoed across the depleted earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.13,0:18:06.48,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Sesah mufeneh enim oyavee eewoo.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.83,0:18:12.73,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,A call for purification, \Npassed down for countless millennia.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.89,0:18:20.31,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Vanoh oo oah vanokeh
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.83,0:18:25.07,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,effzoh keffay wekiyoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.07,0:18:28.14,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Chasing away calamity, purging blight...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.14,0:18:32.75,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,A prayer to purify \Nall wickedness in creation.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.74,0:18:38.57,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,A call for a great cleansing...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.93,0:19:15.42,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,That should do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.71,0:19:20.20,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,What did you think, Sera?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.84,0:19:25.85,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Sera...?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.67,0:19:32.46,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Why are you crying?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.82,0:19:42.79,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That makes 30.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.66,0:19:57.64,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,The idea of a Lavillant woman planting \Ntrees would've been unheard of.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.82,0:20:00.34,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,But it's not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.83,0:20:03.60,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,That said, I wasn't expecting \Nsuch a mystic ritual to be
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.60,0:20:06.23,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,followed by this kind of group work.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.85,0:20:09.53,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You look puzzled.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.02,0:20:14.82,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Veor? Well, I was just thinking \Nabout how ordinary this all seems.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.82,0:20:19.48,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You're right. Healing a \Nforest takes ordinary work.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.48,0:20:24.50,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,But if we don't attend to this ordinary \Nwork, then the forest will be lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.83,0:20:26.14,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Which will cause trouble
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.14,0:20:28.55,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,for our children, grandchildren, \Nand future generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.24,0:20:32.75,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The sentiment that only \Nour individual concerns,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.75,0:20:36.45,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,in the present, are what matter...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.45,0:20:39.93,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Is a rejection of our shared fate \Nis what gives rise to the blight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.26,0:20:44.76,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Fiends are the avatars of \Ngreed and self-interest.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.61,0:20:49.76,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,In this current case, the willpower of \Nthe land was being drained for the spell,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.76,0:20:52.02,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,and after having become unstable,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.23,0:20:57.90,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,the land, in return, drained the \Ncaster of their memories and will.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.90,0:21:02.45,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It takes all that in return? \NThat sounds severe.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.79,0:21:04.40,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,It certainly is.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.40,0:21:08.91,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Severe enough to wipe the memory and \Npersonality of the one involved.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.91,0:21:13.08,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Then Malcius' memories being lost...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.08,0:21:15.50,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Yes, that was the cause.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.50,0:21:16.92,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,I mentioned a bit about this earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.27,0:21:19.75,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,but this would normally be enough \Nto leave someone a shell...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.75,0:21:21.47,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Rarely is someone\N lucky enough to be freed
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.47,0:21:23.55,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,before they are fully drained.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.55,0:21:27.93,Main,Roth,0,0,0,,Such individuals are typically \Nsaid to have been cleansed.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.39,0:21:32.79,Main,Malcius,0,0,0,,Barbarian girl...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.89,0:21:36.23,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Your said your name was Malcius.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.83,0:21:42.04,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,That's the name given to children \Nraised in the orphanage
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.04,0:21:46.42,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,attached to the \NOrder of Commoneras' Malcius Abbey.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.65,0:21:51.50,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I honestly think you're better \Noff forgetting what would've
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.50,0:21:53.23,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,led you to being taken in
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.23,0:21:56.10,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,by that country's orphanage \Nand what you went through there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.91,0:22:00.83,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,You should focus on \Nplanting those saplings.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.13,0:22:04.17,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,That's another kind of cleansing.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.14,0:22:14.81,Sign_Basic,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an9\fad(750,450)\shad0\fs11\bord1\c&HBACBD0&\3c&H506972&\b1\blur1\pos(606,260)}Translation: Lee Francis\N\NTiming: Andy Ellis\N\NEditing: Zachary Carlysle\N\NQuality Control: Salem Alabanza\N\NTranslation Check: Sho Stifler
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.51,0:22:20.11,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Say, Veor...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.97,0:22:27.29,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I think I know why you all consider \Nthe blight so wretched, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.13,0:22:29.47,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.47,0:22:30.62,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.74,0:22:36.20,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,The east... the relationship between \Nthe people here, and nature...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.73,0:22:41.21,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,I think I understand what you're fighting,\Nand trying to accomplish, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.65,0:22:47.83,Main - Top,Veor,0,0,0,,I see.

